WEBVTT

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:05.980
<b>Shimogamo Yaichiro</b>

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.590
Where are the tanuki in contemporary society

00:00:05.590 --> 00:00:09.430
who genuinely aspire to be Nise-emon?

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:13.320
<b>Electric Brandy</b>

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.900
The life of a tanuki, tied down 
by nothing, free as a bird

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:18.990
and the life of Nise-emon, being 
roused day or night for any trouble,

00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.000
having to take charge of all manner of things.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.720
Weighing these options, upstanding 
tanuki ask themselves,

00:00:29.070 --> 00:00:33.090
"The traditional title of Nise-emon 
is certainly an honor,

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:39.390
but is taking it worth throwing away 
this easy, comfortable lifestyle?"

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:45.100
The day Nise-emon will be decided, that is to say, 
the anniversary of our dad's death...

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:51.730
That is to say, the day of the detestable 
Friday Fellows' year-end bash, had arrived.

00:02:22.990 --> 00:02:25.990
<b>Episode 10: 
The Behind-the-Scenes 
Dealings of Ebisugawa Soun</b>

00:02:27.170 --> 00:02:28.710
Oh, Yasaburo.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:31.130
The world is full of surprises.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:34.210
You're up stupid early, too, huh.

00:02:34.210 --> 00:02:35.750
You fool.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:40.730
I'm always up this early to 
strengthen my mind.

00:02:40.730 --> 00:02:43.920
You just didn't know because you 
laze around sleeping all morning.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.980
Nise-emon is one who should shoulder 
the future of tanuki society.

00:02:50.240 --> 00:02:54.280
Whoa, whoa, that's pretty serious 
for first thing in the morning.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:03:00.420
The tanuki who'll be chosen as Nise-emon must be worthy of that great role.

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:04.610
That's why I've been putting in so 
much hard work, in my own way.

00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:05.710
I see.

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:09.620
I admire your resolve.

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:14.040
It's great to have a magnificent 
ideal. However--

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:17.360
No, it's fine. Don't say anything.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:21.040
I may not know everything, but 
I know what you're thinking.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:24.940
You can probably read my thoughts, too.

00:03:25.310 --> 00:03:28.260
I might really be an idiot.

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:33.790
I might just be idealizing Father.

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.730
It seems like that's exactly 
what Uncle's thinking.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:43.360
Tanuki society might not even care 
about Nise-emon anymore.

00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:44.720
But,

00:03:45.150 --> 00:03:50.250
how else can I fulfill my 
dream of being like Dad

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:53.460
besides becoming Nise-emon?

00:03:53.990 --> 00:03:58.520
You've been waking up early every 
morning to think about that?

00:04:01.190 --> 00:04:03.840
You should sleep in once in a while.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.760
You might be right.

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.420
Are you going to see the elders today?

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:13.710
Yeah.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:16.400
If I don't meet with them,

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:19.910
they'll consider me as having abandoned 
my will to become Nise-emon.

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:23.690
By the way, Kaisei was 
saying something weird.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:24.750
What?

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:26.070
"I'm sorry."

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.610
What could that be about?

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:30.560
The Ebisugawas might do something...

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:32.960
How stupid!

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.870
If those idiot brothers try anything,

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:40.580
it'll end with me chomping their butts and hurling them into the cold Kamo River.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.660
We'll that's some great 
spirit you have there,

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:46.920
but at the critical moment you always 
reveal your true, hopeless self.

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.390
Don't be a smart-aleck!

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.240
I'm just worried about you!

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:51.860
Don't fight!

00:04:55.820 --> 00:04:59.410
I'm going to Nanzenji, and then 
after meeting with the chief

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.610
I'll head to Sensuiro in the evening 
with my supporters.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:06.880
We'll prepare the banquet at Akegarasu,

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.580
so come once the election is over.

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:10.700
Okay.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:13.000
What'll you be up to, Yasaburo?

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:16.230
I think I'll go over to Yajiro's.

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.090
Today's the day Dad died,

00:05:19.450 --> 00:05:22.590
so it'd be sad to leave him on his own.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:24.410
In that case, Yasaburo,

00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:28.430
please also remind the owner of 
Akegarasu we're coming.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.430
Okay.

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.320
Well then, I'll be going.

00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:38.690
Remember,

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:42.090
you're Shimogamo Soichiro's son!

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:44.110
Go get 'em!

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.540
I know, Mother.

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:50.640
In the end it all comes down to chance.

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.780
Yeah.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:55.410
Okay, Mother, I'm off.

00:05:55.410 --> 00:05:57.530
Look forward to good news!

00:05:57.530 --> 00:05:58.800
Hey,

00:06:00.560 --> 00:06:02.090
be careful.

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:22.330
Organize and pack up the old switchboards 
piled in Old Warehouse No. 1.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:26.110
Don't cut any corners, 'cause 
we'll be checking your work.

00:06:29.590 --> 00:06:33.870
<b>Old Warehouse No. 1</b>

00:06:31.140 --> 00:06:33.870
Okay, okay, we need you 
to get going right away.

00:06:34.110 --> 00:06:38.960
We have to prepare for tonight starting this afternoon, so we're really busy.

00:06:38.960 --> 00:06:44.390
We can't leave until we see 
that you've gotten started.

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:55.960
Sometimes cell phone signals cause the switchboards and old machinery to start up.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:06:57.710
We can't have you getting hurt.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:07:00.240
So you should leave your phone over there.

00:07:13.140 --> 00:07:16.060
I knew it! The Shimogamo kids are such idiots.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.470
There's a saying, "Carelessness 
is one's greatest enemy."

00:07:18.470 --> 00:07:22.000
Can I use it now? 
Can I make it buzz?

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:24.860
Stay cool, Ginkaku.

00:07:25.220 --> 00:07:28.300
That's for after we figure out where Yaichiro is.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.150
And I wonder where Kaisei went.

00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.730
If she butts in the plan'll go up in smoke.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:39.070
Once we nab Yaichiro and his mom, 
that leaves Yasaburo, huh.

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:40.890
He's gonna be a pain.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:45.530
Don't be a baby. Plus, Father 
should catch him for us.

00:07:45.530 --> 00:07:48.050
Even if he fails, I'll figure out something.

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.540
You're really in your element, huh.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:54.490
So in it, you're freaking me out.

00:07:55.120 --> 00:07:58.080
By the way, what'll we do 
about the frog in the well?

00:07:58.320 --> 00:08:03.200
We can just leave him be. 
He can't do anything.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.870
Hey!

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:09.210
Hey, somebody! Open the door!

00:08:14.070 --> 00:08:17.050
What's going on? Something smells amazing.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.600
Heyo!

00:08:19.010 --> 00:08:22.770
It's your share of the Christmas 
Eve fried chicken.

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:24.840
Oh, Yasaburo!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:28.030
Chicken! Well this is lavish.

00:08:28.030 --> 00:08:29.570
It's tender!

00:08:29.570 --> 00:08:33.030
Eating insects all the time 
must be rough on your mouth.

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:38.680
A frog in a well getting to eat fried chicken--

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:41.790
I really appreciate it!

00:08:42.260 --> 00:08:46.870
I'm convinced a little brother is 
something everyone should have.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:50.420
Tonight's the night, Big Brother.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:53.130
The next Nise-emon will be decided.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:56.330
I hope things calm down after that.

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.780
I feel bad for Yaichiro, saying this,

00:08:59.780 --> 00:09:04.330
but I feel like I don't really care 
 who becomes Nise-emon.

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:08.800
As long as things calm down in tanuki 
society, isn't that good enough?

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:12.470
It's been years since Father died, you know?

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.780
Yeah.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:18.730
All I've been thinking about 
since this morning is Father.

00:09:18.730 --> 00:09:20.410
That goes for all of us.

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:23.390
Well, yeah, especially today.

00:09:24.020 --> 00:09:27.020
I try so hard to remember

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:30.940
what Dad's last words were.

00:09:30.940 --> 00:09:35.760
But no matter how often I go through that 
night's events, my memory cuts out partway.

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:40.310
Even as a frog it's painful to think that

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.400
I might go on living my whole 
life without ever remembering.

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:46.630
Big Brother,

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.690
have you seen Kaisei lately?

00:09:51.090 --> 00:09:54.900
Now that you mention it, she 
hasn't come around lately.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:09:57.070
Did you have a fight or something?

00:09:57.070 --> 00:10:01.450
Well, we always fight, but 
she's being a bit weird.

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.080
What do you mean, "weird"?

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:07.060
"I'm sorry." <i>Kaisei</i> said that.

00:10:07.060 --> 00:10:09.140
Don't you think that's strange?

00:10:09.140 --> 00:10:12.170
It does seem strange...

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.250
Right? There's something creepy about it.

00:10:15.250 --> 00:10:18.990
Now that you mention it, 
there've been times

00:10:18.990 --> 00:10:22.110
when Kaisei's been humble 
like that talking to me.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:25.390
After talking for a bit she'll clam up...

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:30.630
like she's got something on her mind. 
I wonder what it could be...

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.020
I don't know what Kaisei is thinking.

00:10:34.020 --> 00:10:36.150
She's a weird one.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:39.090
She certainly is.

00:10:39.390 --> 00:10:44.290
But when she found out I 
was unable to change back

00:10:44.290 --> 00:10:47.060
she cried by the edge of 
the well for a long time.

00:10:47.930 --> 00:10:49.920
She has a kind side.

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.670
Are you still stuck on her?

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:03.090
That's not something to ask a frog in a well.

00:11:03.090 --> 00:11:05.470
I'll just get depressed.

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.910
Sorry, Big Brother.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:12.480
But Kaisei sure is acting strange.

00:11:13.250 --> 00:11:18.030
The view from the bottom 
of a well may not be much,

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.910
but you <i>can</i> see the sky 
and the stars really well.

00:11:21.150 --> 00:11:25.300
My world is small, but since I'm looking 
up at space night after night,

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:27.950
you could say I'm a frog 
on a universal scale.

00:11:28.260 --> 00:11:34.190
When you gaze at space like that all alone, the back of your mind goes quiet

00:11:34.190 --> 00:11:36.510
and you feel as though you've gained an extraordinary amount of wisdom.

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:40.920
If I were to give you my opinion as a wise frog,

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:46.150
it seems like something really 
awful is gonna happen.

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:51.350
What the heck!

00:11:52.970 --> 00:11:54.500
This wind is insane!

00:11:54.900 --> 00:11:57.360
Can't feel it down here, but...

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:03.490
Raijin, god of thunder, has arrived.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.870
This is bizarre.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.120
Seems like someone used the 
Fujin Raijin folding fan.

00:12:09.970 --> 00:12:13.410
Dammit, I wonder where they found it.

00:12:13.410 --> 00:12:16.010
Take care of Mother, Yasaburo.

00:12:16.010 --> 00:12:17.560
This again?

00:12:17.560 --> 00:12:21.930
How useless do I have to be 
before I'll be happy?

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:25.140
A frog in a well can do nothing...

00:12:25.930 --> 00:12:29.730
Well, I can't do anything about that.

00:12:29.730 --> 00:12:33.140
It's okay, Big Brother. Leave it to me!

00:12:33.370 --> 00:12:37.170
Be careful, Yasaburo. I have 
a bad feeling about this.

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.280
Right!

00:12:47.020 --> 00:12:48.270
Mother.

00:13:09.970 --> 00:13:12.970
<b>Shimogamo Jinja</b>

00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:19.310
Mother!

00:13:19.810 --> 00:13:21.310
She's not here?

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:26.470
Mother!

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:42.750
Mother?

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:45.340
It's me, stupid.

00:13:45.920 --> 00:13:49.090
You-- what are you doing here?

00:13:49.090 --> 00:13:51.210
I've been looking for you all this time!

00:13:51.560 --> 00:13:55.810
My brothers are keeping watch, so 
I was hiding behind Kiyomizu-dera.

00:13:56.190 --> 00:13:59.730
Even if you wait here, no one will come.

00:13:59.730 --> 00:14:02.090
My big brothers summoned Raijin

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:05.900
and the Ebisugawa Elite Guard carried 
off your mom a bit ago.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:08.360
Yashiro is probably at the factory.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:11.240
Yaichiro has been captured by now.

00:14:11.470 --> 00:14:15.200
My dad means to boil him in a hot pot!

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:17.870
Just like Uncle.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:24.320
It's true, the one who made 
Uncle into a hot pot was...

00:14:24.660 --> 00:14:26.390
my dad.

00:15:33.500 --> 00:15:35.030
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.090
Big Brother!

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:46.530
And I hope Prof. Akadama is in good health?

00:15:46.530 --> 00:15:49.920
Unfortunately, I haven't seen him lately.

00:15:49.920 --> 00:15:54.340
Even though you got along so well? 
Is there some kind of problem?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.260
Hmm.

00:15:56.780 --> 00:15:59.070
If there's a problem,

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:01.980
I guess we should say it's mine.

00:16:01.980 --> 00:16:04.970
Is that so?

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:10.490
But I have some great memories of the 
things we learned from Prof. Akadama.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.460
Yeah, we were both so young.

00:16:13.460 --> 00:16:16.580
And then we both fell 
for the same tanuki.

00:16:16.580 --> 00:16:20.640
Ah, remembering it now, 
that was pretty cute.

00:16:21.090 --> 00:16:23.370
Cute?

00:16:23.710 --> 00:16:28.460
But it sure went fast, huh. 
You got married just like that.

00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:32.540
Really? It didn't feel that way for me.

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:37.600
It does to me... because I entered 
the Ebisugawa family right after.

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:44.600
So it's from that time, then, that 
our relationship has been strained...

00:16:45.120 --> 00:16:49.300
And then I lost the Nise-emon election.

00:16:49.660 --> 00:16:51.770
I wonder why.

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:58.070
I made a vow, then.

00:16:59.770 --> 00:17:02.370
Did you make good on it?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:07.080
No, but it won't be long now.

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:09.760
Oh, well that's what's most important.

00:17:09.760 --> 00:17:11.940
It's thanks to you.

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:15.450
I must have made things difficult for you.

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:19.600
No worries, isn't that all ancient history?

00:17:19.820 --> 00:17:23.980
It's not an exaggeration to say I'm a great tanuki now, too, and I have children.

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:26.740
I'm not hung up on the little things.

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.970
I'm happy to hear you say that.

00:17:28.970 --> 00:17:31.230
You certainly have made 
something of yourself.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:34.310
Now now, so have you.

00:17:35.870 --> 00:17:37.910
There's something over there.

00:17:38.310 --> 00:17:40.330
Looks like a cage, but...

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:45.130
It does seem like a cage. Should 
I have them take it away?

00:17:45.130 --> 00:17:47.340
No, it's not so serious as that.

00:17:47.340 --> 00:17:49.950
Just a strange thing to leave around.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:55.880
Drunk, huh, Big Brother.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:18:00.830
No need to worry about me. 
I don't get dead drunk.

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:05.470
If you say so. But before we continue I'd like to have a reconciliation ceremony.

00:18:05.470 --> 00:18:07.940
I even invited some witnesses.

00:18:07.940 --> 00:18:11.020
Once we've exchanged official 
promises that we've made up,

00:18:11.020 --> 00:18:13.670
we can drink without a care.

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.240
You're really blowing this up.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:18.780
Can't we just settle it between you and me?

00:18:18.780 --> 00:18:20.660
I don't think so.

00:18:20.660 --> 00:18:24.290
We're pillars of tanuki society.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:27.290
So, I'd like to get this done once and for all.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:29.790
Okay, I see what you mean.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.210
The witness!

00:18:38.780 --> 00:18:40.830
As a witness,

00:18:40.830 --> 00:18:44.530
we are graced with the presence 
of Suzuki Satomi.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:56.470
Suzuki, for what purpose are you here?

00:18:56.830 --> 00:19:00.330
Because you never ever come to see me.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:05.470
But I don't understand. What's the idea?

00:19:05.470 --> 00:19:08.260
I'm joining the Friday Fellows.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:21.510
I see. And you need me for that, huh.

00:19:22.240 --> 00:19:24.780
It's a big help that you catch on so quickly.

00:19:25.160 --> 00:19:28.670
A seat opened up in the Friday Fellows

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:33.400
and in order to fill it, I need to 
procure hot pot ingredients.

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:39.820
Does the professor know?

00:19:40.370 --> 00:19:45.200
Oh, how pitiful you are. Master 
doesn't know anything.

00:19:48.200 --> 00:19:52.430
Farewell, Big Brother. I doubt 
I'll be seeing you again.

00:19:52.430 --> 00:19:56.540
As my little brother, you're okay with that?

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:07.850
I'm sorry.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:11.290
I thought it was something like that.

00:20:11.990 --> 00:20:16.360
I just thought it for so long that 
I'm actually surprised now.

00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:18.740
Let me go, agh!

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:19.940
What happened?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:23.320
<b>Ebisugawa</b>

00:20:21.550 --> 00:20:23.320
Yasaburo!

00:20:25.370 --> 00:20:28.520
Don't worry about what Kaisei said.

00:20:28.520 --> 00:20:33.820
When she's half asleep she loses track of the line between dreams and reality.

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:37.540
She's delicate because I raised 
her so carefully, you know.

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.120
Whatever tonight's outcome,

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:44.480
I'd been thinking to hold a banquet and 
invite the Shimogamo family.

00:20:44.770 --> 00:20:47.380
All the members of both families are there already.

00:20:47.380 --> 00:20:50.970
You were the only one we couldn't find.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.080
I appreciate the invite,

00:20:53.080 --> 00:20:56.440
but we booked Akegarasu for tonight.

00:20:56.440 --> 00:21:00.020
Oh you don't know, huh. 
That plan was scrapped.

00:21:02.470 --> 00:21:05.830
I'm sopping wet and have no manners,

00:21:05.830 --> 00:21:08.880
so I'd like to beg off on attending 
your auspicious gathering.

00:21:08.880 --> 00:21:11.740
Either way you can't escape.

00:21:11.740 --> 00:21:14.090
It would be stupid to get hurt.

00:21:14.090 --> 00:21:16.240
Don't make us waste our time.

00:21:17.170 --> 00:21:19.060
Stay away from me!

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:22.610
Anybody who comes near me gets my 
teeth through one side of their ass!

00:21:23.980 --> 00:21:26.450
There are all sorts of goodbyes.

00:21:27.100 --> 00:21:29.340
There are sad goodbyes,

00:21:29.340 --> 00:21:33.380
and sometimes goodbyes you're thankful 
for, that take a load off of your mind.

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:35.970
It often happens that someone 
you said goodbye to

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:39.480
unexpectedly returns, all self-conscious.

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:44.630
Then there are times when, anticipating that, 
you put up the front of a short goodbye,

00:21:44.630 --> 00:21:47.200
only to have them not return so soon.

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:51.190
And then there are goodbyes 
that last forever,

00:21:51.190 --> 00:21:55.580
true goodbyes that only 
happen once in your life.

00:23:31.090 --> 00:23:33.760
Oh no! It doesn't seem 
like I'm gonna be rescued!

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:36.390
This sucks, but there's nothing 
I can do from inside this cage!

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:39.120
Whither the fate of our family?!

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Back in the Game</b>
